FORM K-1.
IN THE MATTER OF: reconsideration.

OFF THE RECORD: The motion to reconsider is the only mercy in the
OFF THE RECORD: building, and it is priced accordingly. While the
OFF THE RECORD: motion is on file, a verdict that would issue is
OFF THE RECORD: intercepted, exactly once per case: the dossier is
OFF THE RECORD: impounded as the filing fee, the pending appeals are
OFF THE RECORD: dismissed with it, the sealed particulars are filed
OFF THE RECORD: as the grounds, and the proceedings resume at the
OFF THE RECORD: named article. The second offense is final.

ARTICLE 1.
    FILE A MOTION TO RECONSIDER, REFERRING TO ARTICLE 2, THE GROUNDS FILED UNDER grounds.
    PROCLAIM "About to consult a record that was never made.".
    PROCLAIM the-missing-record.
    PROCLAIM "This line is never reached; the verdict intercepted it.".

ARTICLE 2.
    PROCLAIM "The motion is granted. The Court will not do this twice.".
    PROCLAIM "The grounds, unsealed: " PLUS grounds.
    ADJOURN INDEFINITELY.
